    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d444">

                <pb facs="0773" n="763" xml:id="pg763"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/10–1446: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Acting Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1946-10-14T00:00:00+01:00">October 14,
                            1946—midnight</date>.<lb/>[Received October 14—10:05 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>5169. For Acheson and Vincent from the Secretary.<anchor n="71" xml:id="d444-f1"
                    /> Bevin<anchor n="72" xml:id="d444-f2"/> has told me that British have received
                    request from Chinese for purchase of arms. Bevin has issued instructions that
                    sales are not to be made. [Byrnes.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d444-f1" n="71" xml:id="d444-f1-content">
                <p>Secretary of State Byrnes was attending Meeting of Foreign Ministers in
                    Paris.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d444-f2" n="72" xml:id="d444-f2-content">
                <p>Ernest Bevin, British Secretary of State for Foreign Affairs.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
